==============================================================================
VI. ODD TANGENTS WORTH NOT FORGETTING
==============================================================================
1. Autocorrelation is the honest Fejer object: Q is its Fourier transform.
   J_3 is not raw autocorrelation; it is an oriented wedge fold of it.
2. Interval maximizes IPR and J_3 variance together at p=13, but p=7,11
   show the old anti/locality regime: localization helps packing before it
   helps total H.
3. Single flips usually destroy the Fejer peak and the J_3 gradient in the
   same direction. This is a finite-difference version of rearrangement.
4. The next proof object may be a pinned-exclusion expansion: start with
   spectral pinned walk counts, then subtract repeated-vertex diagrams.
